Z||000000||danny boy||03-03-2001||12:35 PM|||| Soon my car will have '88 rear suspension and thus,'88 brakes.I will probably have Gramd Am brakes on the front. If I use the origional '87 master cyl,will I be OK? Should I go to the '88 mastercyl(I have one) or should I look at something else?<BR> The reason I'm purtting G/A brakes on the front is mainly for looks. Rear vented rotors and solid front ones are going to look pretty bad through 17" wheels.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||03-03-2001||04:46 PM||||I haven't done the math on the 88. I don't have the caliper specs handy. I can look at this next week. You'll have to get me the diameter of the 88 rear pistons before I can run the numbers. If you have excel97 or later you can download the spread sheet and drop the number in that and it will do most of the math for you. <P>For a rough guess...<P>At the very least you may have to alter the plumbing of the MC so that the quick takeup outlet is feeding the front brakes.<P>This is a fairly sticky one. Untill I do the math I can't really say what will happen with the 88 calipers on the older MC. You'll loose power but how much I don't know.<P>The GA calipers are going to give you an increase up front. If you put them on the 24mm MC it could be too much.<P>reproportioning the system will be very interesting. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||danny boy||03-03-2001||09:07 PM||||  Currently, The front hubs are at the machine shop and the cradle adapters aren't ordered yet. The project should be done before april, though. I'll keep you updated.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ironhedno3||03-04-2001||04:20 PM||||use the master cylinder for a 1990 full size blazer..if you have a sunroof swap resiviors ||||reg||6
Z||000004||theogre||03-04-2001||04:34 PM||||Actually, that's probably not what should be done here. If you put the 28mm blazer MC on it, I expect the 88 rear caliper to do the same thing earlier years OE rear would do... loose allot of braking power. The 88 rear will aready loose some whan used on the 25.4mm MC.<P>What is most likely to be needed is to cross the lines between the MC and balance block so that the big GA front caliper can make use of the Quick Take-up piston in the MC. You'll have to make lines to do this.||||reg||1
Z||000005||danny boy||03-04-2001||06:02 PM||||Heres what I think I'm gonna do-<BR>I will be using an 88 MC, quick takeup on the G/A fronts, and a proportioning valve. As I said, this car is for looks,but safety is always the number 1 concern.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||03-04-2001||10:57 PM||||That should work. actually you may need to remove/alter the spring in the OE prop valve. I'd see what that does before adding a new valve.||||reg||1
